e x 2.5cm tall. Text layout:\n   - Title \"Frozen VLA\" in 11pt bold serif, navy color\n   - Subtitle \"0.4–3.6B params\" in 8pt sans-serif, gray (#7F8C8D)\n   - Small lock icon or snowflake symbol indicating \"frozen\"\n   - A subtle \"NO gradient\" annotation in 7pt italic gray below\n\n4. Arrow pointing right, splits into K=2 parallel thin arrows (dashed, #7F8C8D).\n\n5. \"K Action Candidates\" region: two small action vector boxes stacked vertically, each 1.2cm x 0.6cm:\n   - Top box: light coral fill (#FADBD8), text \"a_1\" in 9pt\n   - Bottom box: light teal fill (#D5F5E3), text \"a_2\" in 9pt\n   - Label \"K=2 samples\" in 8pt gray below\n\n6. Arrow pointing right, converges.\n\n7. \"Argmin Centering\" box: light yellow (#FEF9E7) fill, border (#F39C12, 1.2pt). Size: 2cm x 1.5cm. Text \"Argmin\" in 10pt, subtitle \"select closest to mean\" in 7pt gray. A small mathematical annotation: \"argmin_i ||a_i - a_bar||\" in 8pt italic.\n\n8. Arrow pointing right.\n\n9. \"CRM\" box: warm accent color, fill (#FDEBD0), border (#E67E22, 1.5pt). Size: 2cm x 1.8cm. Text layout:\n   - \"CRM\" in 11pt bold serif, color #E67E22\n   - \"615K params\" in 8pt sans-serif gray\n   - \"1.8 MB\" in 7pt gray\n   An upward arrow from below labeled \"obs features\" in 8pt gray, connecting from the VLA box (showing feature reuse).\n\n10. Arrow pointing right, with a small \"+\" symbol and \"residual delta_a\" annotation in 8pt gray.\n\n11. \"Refined Action\" box: soft green fill (#D5F5E3), border (#27AE60, 1.5pt). Size: 1.8cm x 1.5cm. Text \"Refined Action\" in 10pt serif.\n\nBetween VLA and CRM, draw a thin dashed curved arrow (gray, 0.8pt) from VLA bottom to CRM bottom, labeled \"obs features\" in 7pt italic gray. This shows CRM uses VLA's internal representations.\n\n========================================\nPanel (b) \"Adaptive Gating\" (right top, ~26% width):\n========================================\n\nDecision diagram showing the adaptive K mechanism.\n\nTop: A diamond decision node with text \"L2 distance\" in 9pt. Fill: very light gray (#FAFAFA). Border: navy (#2C3E50, 1.2pt). Size: 2cm x 1.5cm.\n\nBelow the diamond, the L2 formula: \"d = ||a_1 - a_2||_2\" in 9pt italic serif.\n\nTwo branches from the diamond:\n\nLEFT branch (L2 > tau):\n- Arrow going down-left, label \"d > tau\" in 8pt bold, color academic red (#C0392B)\n- Rounded box: fill (#FADBD8), border (#C0392B, 1.2pt). Text:\n  - \"VLA Uncertain\" in 9pt bold, red\n  - \"Apply CRM correction\" in 8pt gray\n  - Icon or symbol: exclamation mark\n\nRIGHT branch (L2 <= tau):\n- Arrow going down-right, label \"d <= tau\" in 8pt bold, color green (#27AE60)\n- Rounded box: fill (#D5F5E3), border (#27AE60, 1.2pt). Text:\n  - \"VLA Confident\" in 9pt bold, green\n  - \"Use argmin directly\" in 8pt gray\n  - Icon or symbol: checkmark\n\nBelow both boxes, a subtle annotation: \"tau calibrated on held-out demos\" in 7pt italic gray.\n\n========================================\nPanel (c) \"Gating Effect\" (right bottom, ~26% width):\n========================================\n\nScatter plot showing trigger_rate vs improvement (delta SR) for 4 LIBERO suites.\n\nAxes:\n- X-axis: \"Trigger Rate (%)\" range 2–9, label in 9pt serif\n- Y-axis: \"delta SR (pp)\" range -1.0 to +3.0, label in 9pt serif\n- Only left and bottom spines, thin (#BDC3C7, 0.8pt)\n- Light horizontal gridlines only (#F0F0F0, 0.5pt)\n\nData points (large circles, 120pt marker size, white fill with colored edge, edge width 2pt):\n- Spatial: x=7.8, y=+2.1, edge color #2C3E50 (navy), label \"Spatial\" in 8pt\n- Goal: x=5.2, y=+1.3, edge color #2980B9 (blue), label \"Goal\" in 8pt\n- Object: x=3.2, y=+0.1, edge color #E67E22 (orange), label \"Object\" in 8pt\n- Long: x=3.8, y=-0.3, edge color #C0392B (red), label \"Long\" in 8pt\n\nLabels placed directly next to each point (no legend box needed).\n\nA vertical dashed line at x=5.0 (thin, gray #BDC3C7, 0.8pt), with annotation on each side:\n- Left side: \"Confident suites\" in 7pt italic gray\n- Right side: \"Uncertain suites\" in 7pt italic gray\n\nA subtle trend: points to the right (higher trigger rate) have higher improvement. The visual story is: \"gating correctly modulates intervention intensity.\"\n\nTitle above: \"Gating Modulates Intervention\" in 10pt serif bold.\n\n========================================\nFORBIDDEN:\n- NO matplotlib default colors (tab10, tab20)\n- NO gray plot background\n- NO thick axis lines\n- NO legend boxes with borders\n- NO Comic Sans or monospace fonts\n- NO 3D effects\n- NO gratuitous gradients\n- NO clipart-style icons\n========================================\n","userModified":false}}
